1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,120
Imagine living in an Indian village…

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:04,930
but to reach the rest of India,
you had to cross Bangladesh!

3
00:00:05,410 --> 00:00:08,200
This actually happened along
the India-Bangladesh border.

4
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,050
These unusual territories
were called enclaves.

5
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:14,460
Some Indian villages were completely
surrounded by Bangladeshi territory,

6
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:15,400
and vice versa.

7
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:16,330
For generations,

8
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,770
these communities faced complicated
problems involving access,

9
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:21,850
administration and basic services.

10
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:25,040
The border was more confusing
than anyone could imagine.

11
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:26,490
But in 2015,

12
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,890
India and Bangladesh exchanged enclaves
under a historic land boundary agreement.

13
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,220
111 Indian enclaves went to Bangladesh,

14
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:36,760
while 51 Bangladeshi enclaves
became part of India.

15
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:39,770
Would you have been able to live in a
village surrounded by another country?

